⚙️ Hyperparameter Tuning

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 What are Hyperparameters?

Hyperparameters are:

* Settings defined before training
* Not learned from data

Examples:

* Learning rate
* Number of neighbors (K in KNN)
* Regularization strength (λ)
* Tree depth
* Number of estimators

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔍 Why Hyperparameter Tuning?

Wrong hyperparameters can cause:

* Overfitting
* Underfitting
* Poor performance

Tuning helps:

* Improve model accuracy
* Optimize performance
* Balance bias-variance tradeoff

---

📌 Hyperparameter Tuning Methods

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1️⃣ Grid Search

How It Works:

* Try all possible combinations
* Select best performing combination

Example:

* K = [3, 5, 7]
* Metric = ["euclidean", "manhattan"]

Tests all combinations.

---

Advantages:

* Exhaustive search
* Finds optimal combination (within grid)

Disadvantages:

* Computationally expensive
* Slow for large parameter space

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2️⃣ Random Search

How It Works:

* Randomly selects parameter combinations
* Tests limited number of combinations

---

Advantages:

* Faster than Grid Search
* Good for large parameter space
* Often performs nearly as well

---

Disadvantages:

* May miss optimal combination

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3️⃣ Bayesian Optimization (Advanced)

* Smart search method
* Learns from previous results
* More efficient
* Used in advanced ML systems

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔗 Cross-Validation + Hyperparameter Tuning

In practice:

* Combine both together
* Use GridSearchCV or RandomizedSearchCV

This:

* Tunes hyperparameters
* Validates using cross-validation
* Selects best model automatically

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 Bias-Variance Tradeoff

Hyperparameter tuning affects:

| Too Complex Model | Too Simple Model |
| ----------------- | ---------------- |
| Overfitting       | Underfitting     |
| Low bias          | High bias        |
| High variance     | Low variance     |

Goal:
👉 Find optimal balance.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚠️ Common Mistakes

* Tuning on test data
* Using very large parameter grid
* Ignoring cross-validation
* Not scaling features
* Over-tuning model

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------0

📌 Best Practices

* Always keep test set separate
* Use cross-validation for tuning
* Start with Random Search
* Narrow grid after first tuning
* Monitor multiple evaluation metrics

